 "top": "ot_hbm_idx_score_quarter_f7",
 "why": "HBM-IDXSQ8 10-20 (owner clock rule 10-20 08:50; landed-regions-standard-1018): the IDX quarter scorer (1.3 x 2.7 mm, 8 x 47k-flop-column leaves) as a LANDED parent. One region per child: W glue, 8 leaves (each the die's chunk clock), E glue. Every W->leaf, leaf->leaf and leaf->E crossing lands in a 2-slot ring (E = K = 1, +2 edges = the old W-pin + E-pin hop cost); the dataflow is a W->E DAG, so the offsets schedule keeps the flat calendar (score +10 edges). Geometry plan (centres, um): leaves 648 sq on a 691.2 pitch, 43.2 landing channels, W/E glue columns 86.4; native32 landings (16-bit kept chunk selectors, reset forest); reset root l01 (centre), hops <= 405 um.",
